# Veripsa release gate (auto-discovered). One gate per file -> two PRs adding gates add two
# FILES, never a shared line -> no false merge conflict on registration. register_gate is
# defined in run_gates.sh. Format: register_gate <test> <marker> <name> <ok_blurb> <desc> [tail]
register_gate "tests/test_builtin_call_stoplist.py" "BUILTIN CALL STOPLIST GATE: PASS" "builtin/short-name call stoplist (false-coupling precision)" "builtin/short-name call stoplist: an un-imported single-definer call to a BUILTIN/STDLIB method name (pop/all/parse/assign/HasPrefix/Do/NewDecoder) or a ≤2-char target (m/a/f/x) no longer false-couples; import-confirmed + domain-name couplings survive (recall-safe); backtest mirror in sync; content-free" "builtin/short-name call stoplist (FALSE-COUPLING audit 2026-06-21, flask/nestjs/hugo: ~8-10% of shipped pairs ~90-100% false): the extractor records a method call by its BARE attribute tail (Promise.all->all, JSON.parse->parse, dict.pop->pop, Object.assign->assign, strings.HasPrefix->hasprefix, sync.Once.Do->do, json.NewDecoder->newdecoder) so a bare builtin name matches a LONE same-name class method and the import-UNCONFIRMED single-definer rule false-couples the caller to that unrelated file; a single-LETTER target even false-couples cross-language. The fix guards the import-UNCONFIRMED single-definer branch ONLY (out_adj/in_adj in _claim_adjacency + calls_h in _dampened_adjacency): drop char_length(target)<=2 AND a builtin/stdlib/container/IO/parse method-name set (CRUD-domain verbs create/build/find/new/save/update/delete/process/validate DELIBERATELY EXCLUDED). RECALL-SAFE -- an IMPORT-CONFIRMED call to these names survives via the EXISTS(imports) branch, domain single-definer names survive. Proven on the live core.main_impact_surface: builtin '.pop()' un-imported = CLEAR, single-letter '.m()' = CLEAR, IMPORT-CONFIRMED '.pop()' = WARN, DOMAIN single-definer = WARN; STRUCTURAL: guard present in all 3 branches, backtest_cochange STOP/MIN_NAME_LEN mirror in sync, CRUD verbs excluded. Recall-safety is also pinned by the existing false_coupling_precision / call_edge_precision / dampened_identity / symbol_use_recall gates staying green. content-free (names only)" 20
